			"Message": "chore(Land): Advance submodules — Consolidate notification handling and improve IPC efficiency\n\nSigned-off-by: Nikola Hristov <Nikola@PlayForm.Cloud>",
			"SHA": "63ea23fe09d1d71e23f202fc6ed7b5c560a6b886"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-28T14:27:00Z",
			"File": [
				"⠇⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				27,
				2
			],
			"Message": "chore(Land): Advance Mountain and Vine submodules — Flatten IPC indirection and consolidate notification surface\n\n**Mountain** (refactor): Eliminate the remaining local wrapper modules in `Source/Vine/Client` and `Source/Cache` that re-exported canonical implementations. Replace all `crate::Vine::Client::*` and `crate::Cache::*` calls with absolute paths `::Vine::Client::*` and `::Cache::*`. Deleted 12+ wrapper modules including `AirServiceProvider`, `AssetMemoryMap::LoadOrInsert`, `PathCanon::Canonicalize`, and all `Vine::Client` atom modules.\n\n**Vine** (refactor): Consolidate the notification `mod.rs` to retain only non-trivial handlers with genuine orchestration complexity. Remove ~25 pure-relay modules (output channel operations, progress lifecycle, webview/extension lifecycle, tree refresh, language settings, workspace edits) that perform single-step delegation — these are now inlined directly in Mountain's dispatcher. Retain only handlers with payload reshaping, channel-drain coalescing, multiple side effects, or non-obvious Sky-event mapping (`OutputChannelCoalesce`, `ProgressStart/End/Report`).\n\nAlso remove the `PublishNotificationFromMux` public module export; the multiplexer read pump now calls `PublishNotification::Fn` directly.\n\nImpact: Mountain's gRPC and caching surfaces are now pure delegations to canonical Vine/Cache definitions. The Vine notification surface is reduced from ~45 to ~20 modules, streamlining the IPC contract while preserving all handlers with genuine orchestration complexity.",
			"SHA": "cb07247c5a89208fed0008dbc6ede12eab64085f"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-28T14:14:22Z",
			"File": [
				"⠁⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				27,
				1
			],
			"Message": "chore(Land): Advance Mountain submodule — Finalize notification relay delegation to Vine\n\n**Mountain** (refactor): Collapse the remaining pure-relay notification handlers in `MountainVinegRPCService` to single-line delegations of `::Vine::Server::Notification::Support::RelayToSky::Fn`. Extension lifecycle, webview lifecycle, language settings, workspace edits, window commands, tree refresh, progress lifecycle, and output channel operations now all route through the canonical Vine relay with `sky://` addressing.\n\nAdd `dev_log!` instrumentation at dispatch sites for `ExtensionDeactivated`, `WebviewReady`, and tree refresh. Remove redundant batch comments as the pattern is now uniform.\n\nImpact: Mountain's notification surface is now a pure routing table. Vine is the single source of truth for all Cocoon→Sky IPC paths, while specialized handlers requiring coalescing, transformation, or state remain in Mountain.",
			"SHA": "cd31d1dc8c89b3694bcd8a0174ea722cc594bf88"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-28T14:08:42Z",
			"File": [
				"⠇⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				27,
				2
			],
			"Message": "chore(Land): Advance Mountain and Vine submodules — Finalize notification delegation to canonical Vine crate\n\n**Mountain** (refactor): Replace the local `super::Notification::*` dispatch with direct calls to `::Vine::Server::Notification::*`, completing the extraction of Cocoon→Mountain IPC logic. All 46+ notification handlers are now thin pass-throughs delegating to the shared Vine library. The `MountainVinegRPCService` is reduced to a pure routing table, with only Mountain-specific utilities (`Support`, `OutputChannelCoalesce`, `TerminalEnvCollection`) retained locally.\n\n**Vine** (refactor): Inline trivial provider unregistration atoms (`UnregisterFileSystemProvider`, `UnregisterUriHandler`) that performed single-step delegation to `UnregisterByHandle`. Retain `UnregisterScmProvider` which contains DJB-31 handle recomputation logic and Sky event relay. Consolidate the unregistration surface to expose only atoms with multi-step orchestration needs.\n\nImpact: Mountain is now a pure composition layer with all Cocoon→Mountain IPC contracts defined canonically in Vine. The provider unregistration pathway is fully symmetrical, and redundant wrapper modules have been eliminated.",
			"SHA": "b08029a42927a463950a743a5ff00ac20245760d"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-28T14:03:20Z",
			"File": [
				"⡇⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				27,
				3
			],
			"Message": "chore(Land): Advance Cache, Mountain, and Vine submodules — Notification delegation completion and provider lifecycle symmetry\n\n**Cache** (docs): Reformat documentation comments in Library.rs to improve readability in source viewers and documentation generators.\n\n**Mountain** (refactor): Complete the systematic decomposition of the gRPC notification surface by delegating all remaining handlers to the Vine crate. Convert `CocoonService` and `MountainService` trait imports to use canonical definitions from `::Vine::Generated`, eliminating local re-exports. The server-side notification modules (`UpdateScmGroup`, `WebviewLifecycle`, `RelayToSky`, provider unregistration) are now thin shims forwarding to `Vine::Server::Notification`. The client-side `Shared` module and stub implementations are reduced to empty pass-throughs, with active code paths using `::Vine::Client::*` directly.\n\n**Vine** (feat): Implement the symmetrical provider unregistration surface — `UnregisterRemoteAuthorityResolver`, `UnregisterScmProvider`, `UnregisterTaskProvider`, and `UnregisterUriHandler` — all integrating with the central `UnregisterByHandle` utility. Add `WebviewLifecycle` notification to canonicalize Cocoon's positional arrays into named-key objects before emitting to Sky renderer channels. Implement `UpdateScmGroup` notification with SCM marker persistence via `VineHost::UpdateScmGroupMarkers` for boot-time replay. Enhance `UnregisterFileSystemProvider` with scheme logging for diagnostic observability.\n\nImpact: Mountain is now a pure composition layer with all Cocoon→Mountain IPC delegated to the shared Vine crate. The provider lifecycle is fully symmetrical with clean disposal pathways, and SCM/webview state persists across page reloads.",
			"SHA": "536326f228c847b9574e31f0f72513ba5cf4e984"
		}
	],
